{
  "case_id": "2018-18-966",
  "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In March 2018, Secretary Ross reinstated a citizenship question that has been asked as part of the census in one form or another for nearly 200 years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, we think that the Respondents' claims are not justiciable because their injuries aren't fairly attributable to the government or subject to APA review. And, secondly, the Secretary acted well within his discretion when he determined that reinstating the citizenship question would provide the best evidence of citizenship."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: On the -- on the illegality, is -- is that a -- a predictive factor? In other words, do we, as our cases have often said, do not assume illegal behavior in establishing standing, but is that simply predictive?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: We've used determinate or coercive effect. In Wayfair, one of the reasons we found the stores, not the states, to be injured is because consumers fail to pay taxes, an illegality under the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Census Bureau",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They told him that if he actually asked the question for 30 -- for 22.2 million people for whom no administrative records existed, he would have got actual answers at 98 percent accuracy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question is whether, if you used the model, it would be greater than 98 percent. It would be 99.5 percent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Secretary of Commerce",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the Secretary concluded was, in the face of uncertainty, he'd rather go with the bird in a hand and ask the question at 98 percent accuracy than an unknown and untested statistical model."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Census Bureau",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And that points out why he preferred asking the question and getting actual answers from 22.2 million people at 98 percent accuracy, because you simply didn't have administrative records for 35 million people, and the bureau had not yet figured out how to do that estimation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But a lot of your argument just do not appear in the Secretary's decision memo."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He considered the benefits. He considered the alternatives. He considered the costs --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Administrative records didn't solve the problem that the Department of Justice was trying to solve, which was getting all of their CVAP data from the same source and covering the same time period."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0001-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there's no evidence in this record that the Secretary would have asked this question had the Department of Justice not requested it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents New York, et al.",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Secretary decided to add this question about citizenship to the 2020 census although the record before him contained uncontradicted and strong evidence that it will cause a decline in the response rate of non-citizens and Hispanics, to the detriment of the states and localities where they live."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Do you -- do you think it wouldn't help voting rights enforcement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Was there anything that showed that the Department would have been aided in either past cases or cases on the drawing board? Any case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Department of Justice actually declined to meet with the Census Bureau people who wanted to meet about it. So there was nothing before the Secretary to say that this survey -- this census information would be an improvement -- there was no comparison at all from the Department of Justice about whether this would be an improvement or not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents New York, et al.",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. UNDERWOOD: What we have -- what we have is that this -- the model hadn't been generated, but what we have is the Census Bureau saying this is like other modeling that we routinely do. We're confident that we can do it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So, if the Secretary said -- has to choose between two things, and, on one, the Secretary knows there's a 98 percent accuracy rate, and as to the other, the Census Bureau says, we're going to create a model, and we don't know how -- we can't give you any statistics, but trust us, it's going to be more accurate than 98 percent, is it arbitrary and capricious for the Secretary to say, I'll go with the 98 percent because that's a known quantity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But the -- the United Nations recommends that countries ask a citizenship question on the census. And a number of other countries do it. Spain, Germany, Canada, Australia, Ireland, Mexico ask a citizenship question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But this takes us back, does it not, if I'm following your argument, to the 22.6 million people who will answer the citizenship question but as to whom there aren't administrative records? That's what you're talking about?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States House of Representatives",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LETTER: Thank you. I'll pass that along to her, Mr. Chief Justice. I want to hit just a couple of points, but one of the ones I want to hit right upfront is something that -- that General Underwood said and I think bears some emphasis, which is the -- remember that the -- the census that we're talking about here is the decennial census provided for in the Constitution, of utmost importance to the House of Representatives. That provision obviously is the ground -- has to be the grounding for the statute that is being applied here. And so anything that undermines the accuracy of the actual enumeration is immediately a problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I thought all the information available, as I understand it, leads to only one answer, and so why isn't that answer sufficient for them to take whatever action they consider appropriate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. LETTER",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LETTER: Our position is that,\none, the Justice Department can get this\ninformation elsewhere, as we know.\nBut, two, you can't undermine the\naccuracy of the actual enumeration in order to\nget information --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "GENERAL FRANCISCO",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL FRANCISCO: Mr. Chief Justice,\nthank you. I'd like to make four points:\nFirst, on the disclosure avoidance\nprotocols, we discussed those at our reply\nbrief at page 17. The bottom line is that\nthose protocols apply to all census data,\nincluding on sex, on age, on race, that the\nDepartment of Justice uses to construct citizen\nvoting age population."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So how much\naccuracy --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "GENERAL FRANCISCO",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b4f4d8944f1-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And under my friend's on the other side's\nposition, you are effectively empowering any\ngroup in the country to knock off any question\non the census if they simply get together and\nboycott it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2018-18-966",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "5b4f4d8944f1e8275771f3dfbfdb31bb010b67e59932e39537ddc34405b8af4b",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-5b4f4d8944f1-95",
